{"id": 6811, "stem": "<div class=\"relative w-full min-w-0 max-w-full self-stretch\" id=\"question-text\"><span><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><mark class=\"bg-transparent dark:text-neutral-100\" data-markjs=\"true\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">A</mark> 78-year-old man with severe dementia is brought to the emergency department due to a daylong history of lethargy, fever, and vomiting.\u00a0 The patient lives in a nursing home, and his caregivers report that he has had poor oral intake over the last week.\u00a0 Medical history is significant for emphysema, heart failure with reduced ejection fraction, hypertension, and diabetes mellitus type 2.\u00a0 On physical examination, the patient is lethargic but arousable.\u00a0 Blood pressure is 60/30 mm Hg and pulse is 120/min and regular.\u00a0 The extremities are warm.\u00a0 Coarse rhonchi are heard over the right lower lung.\u00a0 After receiving several intravenous fluid boluses, the patient is given an intravenous infusion of an agent that increases peripheral vascular resistance, increases blood pressure, and decreases heart rate.\u00a0 Which of the following agents is most likely being described?\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c</p></span></div>", "options": [{"label": "A", "text": "Dobutamine"}, {"label": "B", "text": "High-dose dopamine"}, {"label": "C", "text": "Low-dose epinephrine"}, {"label": "D", "text": "Milrinone"}, {"label": "E", "text": "Phenylephrine"}], "correctAnswer": "E", "explanation": "<div class=\"relative w-full min-w-0 max-w-full self-stretch\" id=\"question-explanation\"><span class=\"\"><div id=\"div_t59911\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><div class=\"group/triggerable\" data-is-open=\"false\"><div class=\"group/draggable\" data-is-draggable=\"true\" data-is-dragging=\"false\"><div class=\"group/resizable relative\" data-is-maximized=\"false\" data-is-resizable=\"true\" data-is-resizing=\"false\"><div class=\"relative max-w-full\"><div aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"pointer-events-none absolute left-0 top-0 bottom-0 w-8 z-10 transition-opacity duration-200 bg-gradient-to-r from-white dark:from-nbme-primary-dark-800 warm:from-egg-sour-50 to-transparent opacity-0\"></div><div aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"pointer-events-none absolute right-0 top-0 bottom-0 w-8 z-10 transition-opacity duration-200 bg-gradient-to-l from-white dark:from-nbme-primary-dark-800 warm:from-egg-sour-50 to-transparent opacity-0\"></div><div class=\"max-w-full overflow-x-auto [&amp;_td]:min-w-[8rem] [&amp;_th]:min-w-[8rem]\"><table class=\"border bg-transparent dark:text-white border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white hover:bg-transparent warm:hover:bg-transparent dark:hover:bg-transparent cursor-default mt-2 mb-3\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><tbody style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><tr class=\"hover:bg-original-nbme-400/10 warm:hover:bg-brown-700/10 dark:hover:bg-white/15\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" colspan=\"4\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><mark class=\"bg-transparent dark:text-neutral-50\" data-markjs=\"true\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">C</mark>ardiovascular effects of adrenergic agonists</strong></p></td></tr><tr class=\"hover:bg-original-nbme-400/10 warm:hover:bg-brown-700/10 dark:hover:bg-white/15\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" colspan=\"4\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><ul class=\"flex flex-col justify-start items-start list-inside list-disc ml-4 mb-4\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><li class=\"mb-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">\u03b1<sub style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">1</sub>: peripheral vasoconstriction, \u2191 SVR</li><li class=\"mb-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">\u03b2<sub style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">1</sub>: \u2191 heart rate &amp; contractility, \u2191 cardiac output</li><li class=\"mb-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">\u03b2<sub style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">2</sub>: peripheral vasodilation, \u2193 SVR</li><li class=\"mb-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">D<sub style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">1</sub>: renal arteriolar vasodilation</li></ul></td></tr><tr class=\"hover:bg-original-nbme-400/10 warm:hover:bg-brown-700/10 dark:hover:bg-white/15\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Agonist</strong></p></td><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Receptorbinding</strong></p></td><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Bloodpressure</strong></p></td><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Heartrate</strong></p></td></tr><tr class=\"hover:bg-original-nbme-400/10 warm:hover:bg-brown-700/10 dark:hover:bg-white/15\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Dobutamine</strong></p></td><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\">\u03b2<sub style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">1</sub> &gt; \u03b2<sub style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">2</sub></p></td><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\">\u2013/\u2193</p></td><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\">\u2191</p></td></tr><tr class=\"hover:bg-original-nbme-400/10 warm:hover:bg-brown-700/10 dark:hover:bg-white/15\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" rowspan=\"2\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Dopamine</strong></p></td><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\">D<sub style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">1</sub> &gt; \u03b2<sub style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">1</sub> &gt; \u03b1<sub style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">1</sub>(low-dose)</p></td><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\">\u2013/\u2193</p></td><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\">\u2191</p></td></tr><tr class=\"hover:bg-original-nbme-400/10 warm:hover:bg-brown-700/10 dark:hover:bg-white/15\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\">\u03b1<sub style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">1 </sub>&gt; \u03b2<sub style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">1 </sub>&gt; D<sub style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">1</sub>(high-dose)</p></td><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\">\u2191</p></td><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\">\u2013/\u2193*</p></td></tr><tr class=\"hover:bg-original-nbme-400/10 warm:hover:bg-brown-700/10 dark:hover:bg-white/15\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" rowspan=\"2\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Epinephrine</strong></p></td><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\">\u03b2<sub style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">1 </sub>&gt; \u03b2<sub style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">2</sub> &gt; \u03b1<sub style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">1</sub>(low-dose)</p></td><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\">\u2013/\u2193</p></td><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\">\u2191</p></td></tr><tr class=\"hover:bg-original-nbme-400/10 warm:hover:bg-brown-700/10 dark:hover:bg-white/15\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\">\u03b1<sub style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">1 </sub>&gt; \u03b2<sub style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">1</sub> &gt; \u03b2<sub style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">2</sub>(high-dose)</p></td><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\">\u2191</p></td><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\">\u2013/\u2193*</p></td></tr><tr class=\"hover:bg-original-nbme-400/10 warm:hover:bg-brown-700/10 dark:hover:bg-white/15\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Isoproterenol</strong></p></td><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\">\u03b2<sub style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">1</sub> = \u03b2<sub style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">2</sub></p></td><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\">\u2013/\u2193</p></td><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\">\u2191</p></td></tr><tr class=\"hover:bg-original-nbme-400/10 warm:hover:bg-brown-700/10 dark:hover:bg-white/15\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Norepinephrine</strong></p></td><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\">\u03b1<sub style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">1</sub> &gt; \u03b2<sub style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">1</sub> &gt; \u03b2<sub style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">2</sub></p></td><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\">\u2191</p></td><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\">\u2013/\u2193*</p></td></tr><tr class=\"hover:bg-original-nbme-400/10 warm:hover:bg-brown-700/10 dark:hover:bg-white/15\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Phenylephrine</strong></p></td><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\">\u03b1<sub style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">1</sub></p></td><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\">\u2191</p></td><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\">\u2193*</p></td></tr><tr class=\"hover:bg-original-nbme-400/10 warm:hover:bg-brown-700/10 dark:hover:bg-white/15\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" colspan=\"4\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">*</strong>Reflex-mediated decrease.</p><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">SVR</strong>\u00a0=\u00a0systemic vascular resistance.</p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div></div></div></div></div><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\">Adrenergic agonists are often used to increase blood pressure in patients with shock.\u00a0 <strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Phenylephrine</strong> is a <strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">selective alpha-1 agonist</strong> with no effect on alpha-2 receptors or beta receptors; it causes peripheral vasoconstriction, resulting in\u00a0<strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">increased systemic vascular resistance</strong> (SVR) and <strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">increased blood pressure</strong>, but it has <strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">no direct effect on the heart</strong>.\u00a0 Drugs that increase blood pressure by increasing SVR are called <strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">pressors</strong> and are most useful in treating <a class=\"hint\" data-exhibit-id=\"exhibit-rtsnse20n22x573fbstynm21\" href=\"#exhibit-exhibit-rtsnse20n22x573fbstynm21\">septic shock</a>.</p><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\">Phenylephrine has indirect effects on the heart mediated via the <strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">baroreceptor reflex</strong>.\u00a0\u00a0<a class=\"hint\" data-exhibit-id=\"exhibit-cknhsqmhm5nsld6xn82cyo1k\" href=\"#exhibit-exhibit-cknhsqmhm5nsld6xn82cyo1k\">Increased blood pressure</a> stimulates firing of aortic and carotid baroreceptors.\u00a0 In response, the CNS\u00a0increases parasympathetic output and\u00a0decreases\u00a0sympathetic output, which causes\u00a0<strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">decreased heart rate</strong> and myocardial contractility.\u00a0 These reflexive changes slightly attenuate the initial increase in blood pressure and lead to overall reduced cardiac output.</p><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">(Choices A and D)</strong>\u00a0 Dobutamine is primarily a beta-1 agonist with partial activity on\u00a0beta-2 receptors\u00a0and minimal effect on alpha receptors.\u00a0 It increases heart rate and myocardial contractility (via beta-1 stimulation) and causes mild vasodilation (via beta-2 stimulation)\u00a0to decrease SVR.\u00a0 Milrinone is not an adrenergic agonist, but it inhibits phosphodiesterase 3 to increase\u00a0myocardial contractility and cause peripheral vasodilation (decreases SVR).\u00a0 The combination of increased myocardial contractility (ie, inotropic effect) and reduced SVR induced by these drugs is most useful in treating <a class=\"hint\" data-exhibit-id=\"exhibit-qy0jalx1l18od7q5qbfgkiwa\" href=\"#exhibit-exhibit-qy0jalx1l18od7q5qbfgkiwa\">cardiogenic shock</a>.</p><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">(Choice B)</strong>\u00a0 Dopamine stimulates dopamine-1 (located primarily in the renal arterioles), beta-1, and alpha-1 receptors, with the relative effects being dose dependent.\u00a0 High-dose dopamine primarily stimulates alpha-1 receptors to increase SVR and blood pressure; ongoing beta-1 receptor stimulation offsets the reflex\u2013mediated decrease in heart rate, leaving the heart rate relatively unchanged.</p><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">(Choice C)</strong>\u00a0 Epinephrine stimulates beta-1, beta-2, and alpha-1 receptors with dose-dependent effects.\u00a0 Low-dose epinephrine primarily stimulates beta-1 receptors, resulting in increased cardiac output due to increased heart rate and contractility.\u00a0 At low doses, the vasodilative beta-2\u2013mediated effects are greater than the vasoconstrictive alpha-1\u2013mediated effects, leading to a slight reduction in SVR.</p><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Educational objective:</strong>Phenylephrine is a selective alpha-1 agonist with no effect on alpha-2 or beta receptors.\u00a0 It causes peripheral vasoconstriction that\u00a0increases systemic vascular resistance and blood pressure.\u00a0 It has no direct effect on the heart but stimulates a reflex\u2013mediated decrease in heart rate and myocardial contractility.\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c</p></span></div>", "educationalObjective": "Phenylephrine is a selective alpha-1 agonist with no effect on alpha-2 or beta receptors.  It causes peripheral vasoconstriction that increases systemic vascular resistance and blood pressure.  It has no direct effect on the heart but stimulates a reflex\u2013mediated decrease in heart rate and myocardial contractility.\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c", "subject": "Pharmacology", "system": "Cardiovascular System", "topic": "Sepsis", "category": "Heart failure and shock", "peerCorrect": 50.0}